<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Teixeira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1587–1641</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Teixeira (c. 1587–1641) was a Portuguese explorer and soldier in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. In 1637–1639 he led an expedition of some 2,000 people in canoes up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belem">Belém</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> and back, the first European journey up the whole river. On the return he claimed land far to the west for Portugal, a claim later used to justify Portuguese control of most of the Amazon basin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-teixeira.jpg" alt="Pedro Teixeira" width="300" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lacobrigo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_Pedro_Teixeira.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
